127
00:03:08,320 --> 00:03:09,380
It gets brutally cold.

128
00:03:09,380 --> 00:03:11,360
But there's one more trick hiding

129
00:03:11,360 --> 00:03:12,780
in the rock itself.

130
00:03:13,480 --> 00:03:14,860
Dusty soil on Mercury is a

131
00:03:14,860 --> 00:03:16,660
terrible conductor of heat.

132
00:03:16,660 --> 00:03:17,440
So the burning heat of the

133
00:03:17,440 --> 00:03:18,960
day only reaches a thin layer

134
00:03:18,960 --> 00:03:19,880
at the top.

135
00:03:19,880 --> 00:03:21,280
Dig down a short distance, and

136
00:03:21,280 --> 00:03:23,280
the extreme swings start to fade.

137
00:03:23,280 --> 00:03:24,660
The surface is violent.

138
00:03:24,660 --> 00:03:25,900
Just beneath it, things are far

139
00:03:25,900 --> 00:03:26,820
calmer.

140
00:03:26,820 --> 00:03:27,580
So if you ever had to

141
00:03:27,580 --> 00:03:29,080
survive on Mercury, you wouldn't hide

142
00:03:29,080 --> 00:03:30,100
on the surface.

143
00:03:30,100 --> 00:03:31,460
You'd hide underground.

144
00:03:31,680 --> 00:03:32,860
Now, I have to be honest

145
00:03:32,860 --> 00:03:34,220
with you about something.

146
00:03:34,360 --> 00:03:35,560
The title of this video says

147
00:03:35,560 --> 00:03:37,180
Mercury is the coldest planet.

148
00:03:37,180 --> 00:03:39,180
And that's the feeling Mercury gives

149
00:03:39,180 --> 00:03:40,820
you. Because no other planet loses

150
00:03:40,820 --> 00:03:42,520
heat this violently while sitting so

151
00:03:42,520 --> 00:03:43,880
close to the Sun.

152
00:03:43,960 --> 00:03:45,800
But if we're talking about the

153
00:03:45,800 --> 00:03:47,560
lowest temperature ever recorded in a

154
00:03:47,560 --> 00:03:48,860
planet's atmosphere,

155
00:03:48,860 --> 00:03:50,540
the record belongs to Uranus at

